===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To intend to cause harm; to bear malice.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1557|authorlink=Henry Howard, Earl of Surrey|first=Henry|last=Howard|chapter=Complaint of a lover that defied Love and was by Love after the more tormented|title={{w|Tottel's Miscellany|Songes and Sonettes}}|passage=Thou blinded God (quod I) forgive me this offence, / Unwittingly I went about, to '''malice''' thy pretence.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1596|authorlink=Edmund Spenser|first=Edmund|last=Spenser|title={{w|The Faerie Queene}}|others=book 6, canto 9, verse 39|passage=Who on the other side did seeme so farre / From '''malicing''', or grudging his good houre, / That, all he could, he graced him with her, / Ne ever shewed signe of rancour or of iarre.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1596|authorlink=Edmund Spenser|first=Edmund|last=Spenser|chapter=A Hymn of Heavenly Love|title=Fowre Hymnes|passage=His pains, his poverty, his sharp assayes, / Through which he past his miserable dayes, / Offending none, and doing good to all, / Yet being '''malic'd''' both of great and small.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1599|authorlink=Ben Jonson|first=Ben|last=Jonson|title={{w|Every Man out of His Humour}}|others=act 5, scene 2|passage=I am so far from '''malicing''' their states, / That I begin to pity 'em.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1609|authorlink=Samuel Daniel|first=Samuel|last=Daniel|title=The History of the Civil Wars|others=book 5, verse 48|passage=A feeble spirited king that governed, / Who ill could guide the sceptre he did use; / His enemies, that his worth '''maliced''', / Who both the land and him did much abuse: / The peoples love; and his apparent right, May seem sufficient motives to incite.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1995|author={{w|Fugazi}}|artist={{w|Guy Picciotto}}|title=Fell, Destroyed|album={{w|Red Medicine}}|passage=Here's a list of side effects / Practice tested / Covering every '''maliced''' angle / For example: / You will sleep forever / You will never sleep again}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2005-05-03|title='He was a mess,' woman says of accused|journal=The Whitehorse Star|url=https://www.whitehorsestar.com/News/he-was-a-mess-woman-says-of-accused|passage=Robert Truswell may have been a belligerent and '''malicing''' man, a jury heard this morning during the trial of George Kieran Daunt.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2018-05-14|first=Kimberley|last=Small|quotee={{w|Marion Hall}}|title=Dancehall was contentious, says Marion Hall|journal=The Jamaica Star|url=http://jamaica-star.com/article/entertainment/20180514/dancehall-was-contentious-says-marion-hall|passage=I haven't '''maliced''' anybody, definitely not. I never used to have friends like that. I had a few who I thought were friends. Even if you have friends, things happen and friendship break up, but you move on. But I still talk to everybody.}}

